From 63409448ad42e3a1b92e550a9aceeccac8c1b749 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 01:14:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ship libusb's LGPL licence alongside the package's own

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; the same gap exists in every libusb-package wheel on PyPI, so this needs a maintainer discussion rather than a drive-by PR]

Every wheel bundles a prebuilt libusb-1.0 shared library built from the
src/libusb submodule, which is licensed under the LGPL-2.1 (see
src/libusb/COPYING). setup.cfg's singular license_file names only
libusb-package's own Apache-2.0 LICENSE, so the built wheel ships a
single notice covering the wrapper alone and never the library it
bundles.

Naming the vendored file in place keeps the patch to setup.cfg alone
and lets it track the submodule: setuptools preserves each
license_files entry's path relative to the project root, so it lands
in the wheel as dist-info/licenses/src/libusb/COPYING.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 setup.cfg | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/setup.cfg b/setup.cfg
index f2c0d6c..19ddb3e 100644
--- a/setup.cfg
+++ b/setup.cfg
@@ -12,7 +12,9 @@ url = https://github.com/pyocd/libusb-package
 author = Chris Reed
 author_email = flit@me.com
 license = Apache 2.0
-license_file = LICENSE
+license_files =
+    LICENSE
+    src/libusb/COPYING
 classifiers =
     Development Status :: 4 - Beta
     Intended Audience :: Developers
--
